xt": "Or 'your faces shall be covered with shame'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}, "current_canonical": true}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 97:7", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "አሌ፡ ለክሙ፡ ኃጥኣን፡ እለ፡ ማእከለ፡ ባሕር፡ ወዲበ፡ የብስ፡ እለ፡ ዝክርሙ፡ እኩይ፡ ዴቤክሙ፡።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [239, 240], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "verse_parser_ok", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch97.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 97, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "Woe to you[a], sinners, who are in the midst of the sea and upon the dry land[b], whose memory is evil against you.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The final clause is difficult. It may mean 'your memory is evil,' 'your memorial is evil,' or 'evil remembrance clings to you.'", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The pairing 'in the midst of the sea and upon the dry land' likely functions as a totalizing image, extending the denunciation everywhere people dwell or travel.", "reason": "cultural_note"}]}, "current_canonical": true}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 97:8", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "አሌ፡ ለክሙ፡ እለ፡ ታጠርዩ፡ *ብሩረ፡ ወወርቀ፡ ዘአኮ፡ በጽድቅ፡ ወትብሉ፡ ብዕልነ፡ ብዕለ፡ ወኮነ፡ ለነ፡ ንዋይ፡ ወአጥረይነ፡ ኵሎ፡ ዘፈቀድነ፡።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [239, 240], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "verse_parser_ok", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch97.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 97, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "Woe to you who acquire silver and gold not by righteousness[a], and say, ‘We have become rich with wealth, and we have acquired possessions[c][b], and we have acquired everything we desired.’", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'not in righteousness'; the phrase may describe either the manner of acquiring the wealth or the moral character of the gain more generally.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'We have become rich with wealth, and we have acquired everything we desired.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'heap up'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}, "current_canonical": true}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 97:9", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወይእዜኒ፡ ንግበር፡ ዘ*ኀለይነ፡ እስመ፡ ብሩረ፡ አስተጋባእነ፡ ወመላእነ፡ መዛግብቲነ፡ ከመ፡ ማይ፡ ወብዙኅ፡ *ሐራስተ፡ አብያቲነ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [239, 240], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "verse_parser_ok", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch97.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 97, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "And now let us do what we planned[a], for we have gathered silver, and we have filled our storehouses like water[d][c][b], and many are the laborers of our houses.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'what we thought' or 'what we devised.' The Ge'ez verb can cover both thinking and planning.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "'Like water' is a literal simile. It likely expresses abundance or overflowing fullness.", "reason": "cultural_note"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "The word rendered 'farmers' may also mean agricultural workers more generally; some uncertainty remains in this clause.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "d", "text": "Or 'farmers of our houses'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}, "current_canonical": true}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 97:10", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "language": "Geez", "text": "ወከመ፡ ማይ፡ ይውኅዝ፡ ሐሰትክሙ፡ እስመ፡ ይትነበር፡ *ለክሙ፡ ብዕል፡ ኧሳ፡ ፍጡነ፡ የዐርግ፡ እምኔክሙ፡ እስመ፡ ኵሎ፡ በዐመፃ፡ አጥረይክሙ፡ ወአንትሙ፡ ለመርገም፡ ዐቢይ፡ ትትወሀቡ።", "pages": [241], "validation": "scan_bounded_candidate_not_approved_transcription", "note": "Unapproved OCR/scan-bounded proposal from the chapter97/98 boundary, not canonical POB source. Preserve critical symbols until the printed apparatus is adjudicated."}, "translation": {"text": "", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": []}, "current_canonical": false}]

